    {
      "v": 6,
      "zh": "然而他们不离开耶罗波安家使以色列人陷在罪里的那罪，仍然去行，并且在撒马利亚留下亚舍拉。",
      "en": "But they did not repudiate[NOTE:1] the sinful ways of the family[NOTE:2] of Jeroboam, who encouraged Israel to sin; they continued in those sins.[NOTE:3] There was even an Asherah pole[NOTE:4] standing in Samaria.",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “they did not turn away from.”",
        "Heb “house.”",
        "Heb “in it he walked.” The singular verb (הָלַךְ, halakh) is probably due to an error of haplography and should be emended to the plural (הָלְכוּ, halekhu). Note that a vav immediately follows (on the form וְגַם, vegam).",
        "Asherah was a leading deity of the Canaanite pantheon, wife/sister of El and goddess of fertility. She was commonly worshiped at shrines in or near groves of evergreen trees, or, failing that, at places marked by wooden poles. These were to be burned or cut down (Deut 12:3; 16:21; Judg 6:25, 28, 30; 2 Kgs 18:4).tn Or “an image of Asherah”; ASV, NASB “the Asherah”; NCV “the Asherah idol.”"
      ],
